 "_UNSOUND_WARNING": "Every field named UNSOUND_* is kept as evidence and must NOT be used as a norm. The repeating-unit measure uses a bar signature of pitch CLASSES plus onsets on a 16th grid, which is right for the MIDI it was built for and too coarse for homophonic vocal writing, where every voice moves on the same beats and two adjacent bars in one key routinely share both. It returns 1-bar units at 89% across the whole corpus \u2014 Palestrina 97%, trecento 99%, Monteverdi 96% \u2014 which is a property of the signature and not of the music. Excluding runs of empty bars moved it from 88.4% to 84.6%, the shape of a fix that is not the fix. The sound measure in this file is the fermata phrase length, and only where composers wrote fermatas.",
