 "_note": "Two measures, and only one of them is comparable across genres. REPEAT UNITS: how many bars pass before the material comes back, found by the same algorithm midi-structure.mjs runs on a MIDI file, so the two can be read against each other. Needs no phrase detection and works on any texture. PHRASES: only where the composer wrote the ends down, which in practice means fermatas in chorales. Rest-based phrase inference was tried and DROPPED: it gave Beethoven a commonest phrase of half a bar at 32.9% and Handel one bar at 60%, because a one-beat threshold catches every small gap and in polyphony one voice rests while the others carry on. Shipping that as a norm would have been worse than shipping nothing. Read the Bach figures with the caveat AGENTS.md already gives: some of the variety in a texted genre belongs to the text rather than to a free choice.",
 "_scores_per_collection_cap": 450,
